    "rationale": "Re-freeze to the reference offline-clone evidence topology used by materials/petfinder and materials/edx: a small pixel-locked visual oracle plus broad per-state source rasters. Supersedes the 2026-08-04T14:30:00Z freeze, which designated all 51 anonymous source-direct states as strict pixel visual_contracts; that yields 2*51+1 = 103 hash-bound visual raw artifacts and exceeds the offline-clone acceptance-evidence schema's 100-artifact ceiling, so it was structurally unreleaseable. Mirroring petfinder (home.{desktop,tablet,mobile} pixel oracle), the pixel-locked visual_contract oracle is reduced to exactly the three home 'loaded' checkpoints (home.desktop, home.tablet, home.mobile) at their frozen 1440x900 / 1024x768 / 390x844 viewports, metric pixel-mae-similarity-v1, threshold 0.995, full-region comparison, zero ignore regions. The other 48 anonymous source-direct states are retained verbatim as top-level frozen source rasters (source_artifact_path + source_artifact_sha256, bytes and digests unchanged from the 2026-08-03.tripit-r1 capture) and are witnessed broadly: every state is rendered in a real headless browser (browser evidence) and its source raster is independently re-hashed by the release audit (independent-audit evidence). No retained oracle threshold, comparison region, viewport, or source digest is altered. The two continuously-animated blog-index states the prior freeze marked acceptance_eligible=false 'reference evidence only' are consequently no longer strict visual contracts; they persist as source rasters, removing the earlier internal inconsistency. Thresholds still derive only from source-side flicker floors (threshold = min(0.995, floor - 0.002)); authenticated surfaces remain evidence_kind=unavailable. This re-freeze reshapes the evidence topology only and introduces no new or altered source pixels."
